From: Wenhao Chai <reselfchai@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:48:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] EasyPPO for PPO: actor-only overlong filter,
 noise-normalized critic loss, critic mini-batches

Opt-in flags porting EasyPPO (arXiv 2609.36802, github.com/EasyPPO/EasyPPO 85bde92):
--actor-only-overlong-filter: responses at --rollout-max-response-len (or finish_reason
length) keep full weight in GAE, advantage whitening and the critic update and are masked
out of the actor loss only, with no token in the token-mean denominator.
--critic-variance-weighted-loss (--critic-variance-weight-beta/-min/-max): per-response
weight 1/max(var**beta, w_min) of the prompt group's rewards, computed on the rollout side
over the whole batch with EasyPPO's compute_prompt_variance_loss_weights (verbatim), and
multiplied into the clipped value loss.
--critic-global-batch-size: the critic trainer's own global batch size (e.g. four critic
optimizer steps per rollout); turns off the shared rollout-side DP schedule so each trainer
schedules its equal-size shard locally.
--value-loss-scale: verl's 0.5 factor on the value loss.

